The attached image (Figure 5 from npj Vaccines) demonstrates how Nano-11 facilitates antigen transport to lymph nodes, a crucial aspect of adjuvant function. The flow cytometry plots (A) show that Nano-11 significantly increases the percentage of ovalbumin (OVA)-positive cells in the draining lymph nodes compared to OVA alone or with aluminum hydroxide (AH) on both day 1 and day 2 post-injection. The bar graphs indicate that Nano-11 leads to a much higher mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA per cell (B) and a greater percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) carrying OVA (C) in the lymph nodes, highlighting its superior efficiency in delivering antigens to key antigen-presenting cells compared to AH.